{
  "kind": "mip0018-case",
  "schema": 1,
  "id": "C06",
  "title": "Minimal OwnerKey (kind 3, no OpenZeppelin) lifecycle: deploy, publish, rename, withdraw (six Null records, one event), withdraw again, revive",
  "demonstrates": "MIP \"Applying records\" on chain: latest value wins (S2); one event with a Null record for each common key (name, symbol, decimals, standards, image, image_sha256) deletes every field, so the token identity is not referenced at all — not listed, in no group, as if it had never been described (S3c); a repeated withdrawal changes nothing (S3b); a later record describes it again with only that field (the revive: name and symbol; decimals and standards do not return, S3d).",
  "conclusion": "after publish: name \"Acme Token\", symbol \"ACME\", decimals 6, standards \"mip-0004\" (group \"ACME\"); after rename: name \"Acme Prime\", symbol \"ACMP\", decimals and standards unchanged (group \"ACMP\"); after withdraw and after withdraw again: no identity and no group (`list`: identities none); final: ONLY name \"Acme Again\" and symbol \"ACMA\" (group \"ACMA\"); the publish payload = MIP Appendix A byte-for-byte, the withdraw payload = header + the six Null records.",
  "mip": {
    "commit": "338ea194bbe7c4e5d1829234a503b7c1b11ebf0f",
    "eventName": "mip-0018:token-metadata[v1]"
  },
  "source": {
    "example": "examples/minimal",
    "contract": "examples/minimal/contracts/OwnerKey.compact",
    "metadata": "examples/minimal/owner-key.metadata.json"
  },
  "notes": [
    "withdrawMetadata() emits one event with a Null record for each of the six common keys; the token never had image or image_sha256, and a Null record for a field without a value has no effect.",
    "Kind 3 has no color, so there is no color lookup: per the MIP \"Lookup\" section a contract token is found by querying the contract's kind-3 events, which is `list` — after the withdrawal it must show no identity for (0x11…, 3) and no group.",
    "OwnerKey renames with setMetadata(name, symbol), so the revive sets name and symbol (10- and 4-byte values: \"Acme Again\"/\"ACMA\").",
    "A Null record that deletes a single key while the other fields stay is shown on chain by C12 (steps s3a-publish and s3a-delete-name, vector S3a).",
    "Every intermediate state is re-checkable: `recheck` lists the contract as of each step's block (`list --to-block`)."
  ],
  "placeholders": {
    "{net}": "network options (Preview: --network preview)",
    "{signer}": "wallet 1's signer options (mnemonic file, wallet cache)",
    "{signer2}": "wallet 2's signer options, with its OWN private-state file",
    "{case}": "this case folder",
    "{out}": "where records and observations are written (Preview: this case folder)",
    "{out:<ID>}": "another case's output folder"
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "deploy",
      "runner": "signer",
      "wallet": "wallet1",
      "argv": [
        "deploy",
        "{net}",
        "{signer}",
        "--adapter",
        "examples/minimal/owner-key.mip0018.adapter.ts",
        "--record",
        "{out}/record.json"
      ],
      "expectExit": 0,
      "submits": "deploy"
    },
    {
